        "title": "Video Chess",
        "extract": "Video Chess is a 1979 strategy video game developed and published by Atari Inc. for the Atari 2600. It is a simulation of the board game chess, in which the goal is to lead an opponent into \"checkmate\" by moving pieces of differing movement ability. The player competes against a computer opponent of eight selectable skill levels and can choose whether to play a standard regulation game or to freely set the starting position of the pieces.",
